# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — safety-critical: keeps secrets and report data out of version control.
# =============================================================================

# Secrets: webhook URLs + Anthropic API key live here, never committed.
.env

# Local project registry: holds machine-specific repo paths (and is user-created
# from orion.toml.example). The committed sample is orion.toml.example, not this.
orion.toml

# State store: contains report history (redacted bodies, but still local data).
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal

# Virtual environments — never commit the local interpreter/site-packages.
.venv/
venv/

# Python build / cache artifacts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/

# OS noise — macOS Finder metadata, never useful in the repo.
.DS_Store

# =============================================================================
# Public-showcase hiding (Horizon P): these files stay on local disk but are kept
# OUT of the public tree. They are internal planning scratch, premature OSS-community
# scaffolding, or design-process artifacts — useful to the developer, not to a cold
# reader of the showcase repo. Untracked via `git rm --cached`, ignored here so they
# don't reappear. (History still contains them; that is the accepted stance.)
# =============================================================================

# Internal AI-pairing instructions (still read locally by Claude Code) + scratch to-do.
CLAUDE.md
tasks.md

# Internal planning corpus: the dense roadmap, kickoff docs, the coupling map, idea/strategy
# notes, the old kickoff archive. CHANGELOG.md + docs/known-issues.md stay tracked as the
# reader-friendly progression/rigor signals.
plans/orion-plan.md
docs/archive/
